---
import { AGENT_PROMPT, AGENT_STEPS, EVALUATE_FIRST, JIRA, PATHS } from '@lib/compare/jira-alternative';
---

<section id="ja-switching" class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="ja-switching-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[680px]">
      <h2 id="ja-switching-title" class="h2">
        What to check before you move.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        Moving issues is the easy part. What decides whether a team can leave Jira is the configuration around them, so
        start with these four.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="ja-eval mt-10 md:mt-14">
      {EVALUATE_FIRST.map((item, index) => (
        <li>
          <span class="ja-eval-n mono" aria-hidden="true">
            {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
          </span>
          <h3 class="h3">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="prose text-base mt-2">{item.body}</p>
          <a
            class="link font-normal text-sm mt-3 inline-block"
            href={item.source.href}
            rel={item.source.href.startsWith('http') ? 'noopener' : undefined}
          >
            {item.source.label}
            <span class:list={['arr', { ext: item.source.href.startsWith('http') }]} aria-hidden="true">
              {item.source.href.startsWith('http') ? '↗' : '→'}
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-14 md:mt-20 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <h3 class="ja-path-title">The bulk path: CSV</h3>
        <p class="prose text-base mt-3">
          Export work items from a Jira search, then use the generic CSV import: map the columns to issue fields, run a
          dry run and read the errors row by row before anything is created.
        </p>
        <a class="link font-normal text-sm mt-3 inline-block" href={JIRA.csvExport} rel="noopener">
          Export search results in Jira
          <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
            ↗
          </span>
        </a>
        <h3 class="ja-path-title mt-10">Not built: a native Jira importer</h3>
        <p class="prose text-base mt-3">
          Nothing reads a Jira site directly, and workflows, automation rules and app data have no place to land. Plan
          to leave them behind.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
        <h3 class="ja-path-title">The guided path: an agent on both sides</h3>
        <p class="prose text-base mt-3">
          Only when one agent can reach your Jira site and Nothing Left. It reads the unresolved work there and creates
          issues here through the documented tools, after you approve the mapping.
        </p>
        <div class="panel mt-5">
          <p class="prompt">
            <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">
              ›
            </span>
            <span>{AGENT_PROMPT}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps-list mt-6 prose text-base">
          {AGENT_STEPS.map(step => (
            <li>
              <strong>{step.title}.</strong> {step.body}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <a class="link text-sm mt-6 inline-block" href={PATHS.mcp}>
          Connecting an agent
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ja-eval {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .ja-eval li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 22px 0 24px 44px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .ja-eval-n {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 25px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .ja-eval {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: 48px;
    }
  }
  .ja-path-title {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  }
</style>
